---
import Container from "@moesegfault/style/astro/Container.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
const root = "https://style.moesegfault.dev";
---
<DocsLayout title="Distribution" description="Versioned static asset paths and update policy for MoeSegFault Style." currentPath="/en/distribution/" locale="en">
  <header class="page-intro"><Container><p class="kicker">DISTRIBUTION</p><h1>Cacheable and predictable.</h1><p class="lede">One build serves npm and the static site. Versioned paths are immutable, while mutable aliases express update intent explicitly.</p></Container></header>
  <section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="paths-title"><Container><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Asset map</p><h2 id="paths-title">Asset directory</h2></div></div><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Pinned URL</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Complete styles</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/css/all.css</code></td><td>Default integration</td></tr><tr><td>Design tokens</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/css/tokens.css</code></td><td>Custom interfaces</td></tr><tr><td>Foundations</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/css/foundation.css</code></td><td>Elements and theme basics</td></tr><tr><td>Components</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/css/components.css</code></td><td>Library component appearance</td></tr><tr><td>Token JSON</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/tokens/tokens.json</code></td><td>Programmatic use</td></tr><tr><td>DTCG JSON</td><td><code>{root}/v0.1.1/tokens/tokens.dtcg.json</code></td><td>Design-tool interchange</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div></Container></section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="strategy-title"><Container><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Strategy</p><h2 id="strategy-title">Choose an update strategy</h2></div></div><div class="asset-grid">
    <article class="asset-card"><h3>Pinned version: production default</h3><p>Contents under <code>/v0.1.1/…</code> never change and may be cached for a long time. Upgrades happen explicitly through code review.</p><CodeBlock label="HTML" code={`<link rel="stylesheet"\n  href="${root}/v0.1.1/css/all.css">`} /></article>
    <article class="asset-card"><h3>Default path: controlled drift</h3><p><code>/colors</code> navigates to the current pinned color page; machines can read <code>/colors/colors.css</code> or <code>/colors/colors.json</code> directly. These paths follow the newest stable release.</p><CodeBlock label="HTML" code={`<link rel="stylesheet"\n  href="${root}/css/all.css">`} /></article>
    <article class="asset-card"><h3>Latest: explicit drift</h3><p><code>/latest/…</code> follows the newest stable release and suits showcases or internal tools that intentionally update automatically.</p><CodeBlock label="HTML" code={`<link rel="stylesheet"\n  href="${root}/latest/css/all.css">`} /></article>
  </div><div class="callout"><h3>Cache contract</h3><p>Pinned version URLs are never rewritten, but GitHub Pages does not expose custom cache headers. Treat latest and default aliases as mutable and revalidate them. CSS and JSON are public static assets and contain no environment configuration or application secrets.</p></div></Container></section>
  <section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="release-title"><Container><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Release</p><h2 id="release-title">Release invariants</h2></div></div><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-number">01</span><h3>Build once</h3><p>npm and remote assets reuse the same generated tokens, avoiding two sources of truth.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-number">02</span><h3>Verify first</h3><p>Type checks, unit tests, static builds, and browser smoke tests pass before publication.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-number">03</span><h3>Never overwrite</h3><p>A released version directory is never rewritten by a later pipeline; fixes ship in a new version.</p></article></div></Container></section>
</DocsLayout>
